## Why This Is Asked
This checks basic cross-account governance, cost visibility, and tag-driven policy work flow in a multi-tenant SaaS.

## Key Concepts
- Tag-based access control and tag requirements
- IAM policy conditions and SCPs
- AWS Budgets linked to resource tags
- Onboarding/teardown automation and rollback

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": ["ec2:RunInstances", "s3:CreateBucket", "lambda:CreateFunction"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "Null": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant_id": "true"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test multi-tenant budgeting across accounts?
- How would you handle existing resources without tenant_id tags?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross‑account backup/restore patterns, data residency, encryption, and auditable workflows. Demonstrates handling of least privilege, cross-account trusts, and automated testing.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- KMS key grants per tenant
- S3 bucket policies and cross-account access
- DR testing and auditing

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::CENTRAL_ACCOUNT_ID:role/BackupWriter"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::CENTRAL_ACCOUNT_ID:role/BackupWriter"},
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject","s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-backups-ACCOUNT_ID",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-backups-ACCOUNT_ID/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::CENTRAL_ACCOUNT_ID:role/BackupWriter"},
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt","kms:GenerateDataKey"],
