## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical, beginner-friendly multi-tenant quota control using AWS SaaS patterns. It tests understanding of API Gateway usage plans, Lambda authorizers, DynamoDB for counters, and EventBridge for automated overage handling, plus testing strategies.

## Key Concepts
- API Gateway usage plans and API keys for tenant isolation
- Lambda authorizers and IAM policy generation
- DynamoDB design: tenantId partition key, windowed counters with TTL
- Exponential backoff, throttling, and automated suspensions
- Basic test strategies: unit, integration, and end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton of a Lambda authorizer that enforces per-tenant quotas
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { apiKey } = event.requestContext.identity;
  const tenantId = await getTenantIdFromApiKey(apiKey);

  // Check remaining quota in DynamoDB
  const quota = await checkQuota(tenantId);

  if (quota.remaining <= 0) {
    return generateDenyPolicy(tenantId);
  }

  // Decrement counter and allow access
  await decrementQuota(tenantId);
  return generateAllowPolicy(tenantId);
};
```
